title: Marvel Super Heroes Cube Drafts
date: 27-06-2026
tags: magic, cube

I don't feel so good, Mr. Stark.

Marvel's come and gone! Snapped away in its golden age. Well, at least we got another cube season out of the deal!

# Trophy Boring Boros
![Deck #1](/images/blogs/msh-drafts/deck1.png)

Our first trophy - and first draft! - was a bog standard Boros deck.

Fast mana would've really helped, but we slammed on the gas starting turn two. With an MDFC and [Oliphaunt](https://scryfall.com/card/ltr/139/oliphaunt), our deck was land light and action heavy. We also had a strong sideboard, especially against a couple artifact decks.

I wanted to test out new card [Batroc](https://scryfall.com/card/msc/49/batroc-the-leaper), but he never showed up. I've really warmed up to the _idea_ of this card - a modern [FTK](https://scryfall.com/card/dmr/120/flametongue-kavu) with a ton of upside in the late game - though that art kicks him out of my cube. Can't wait until he leaps into a Lurrus deck!

# 2-1 Golgari Reanimator
![Deck #2](/images/blogs/msh-drafts/deck2.png)

A mid Golgari reanimator deck. This absolutely has the power to hang - [Entomb](https://scryfall.com/card/dmr/82/entomb)/[Reanimate](https://scryfall.com/card/dsc/155/reanimate) [Archon](https://scryfall.com/card/mh2/75/archon-of-cruelty) ended a game on turn two. We're miserably light on discard though.

You can see a [Sneak Attack](https://scryfall.com/card/dmr/139/sneak-attack) plan hanging out in board. I cut it for consistency and a better midrange game. Still not sure that was the right call, but without any kind of tutoring or even filtering, it felt like it'd land us some real clunky hands.

This was only a 2-1, but I got a personal trophy - we took a match off [Wheeler](https://www.youtube.com/@bwheelermtg)! He was playing [Nadu](https://scryfall.com/card/mh3/193/nadu-winged-wisdom) with a backbreaking [Ephemerate](https://scryfall.com/card/mh1/7/ephemerate) loop, but we managed to crush him out in game three.

# Trophy Esper Bad Flash
![Deck #3](/images/blogs/msh-drafts/deck3.png)

Esper tempo with [Flash](https://scryfall.com/card/a25/57/flash) [Wurm](https://scryfall.com/card/dsc/206/worldspine-wurm) to cheese out some wins.

You can see some reanimator pieces in the sideboard - like the Sneak from the last deck, I'm on the fence about whether I should've brought it in, but I didn't want to clog up my draws too much.

I don't think this deck was _great_, but sometimes you just need to high roll.

# Clean Sweep Rakdos Reanimator
![Deck #4](/images/blogs/msh-drafts/deck4.png)

A solid little red/black reanimator deck with an agro backup plan.

Yet again, the sideboard tells the tale of my cowardice. No [Sneak](https://scryfall.com/card/dmr/139/sneak-attack)/[Emrakul](https://scryfall.com/card/2x2/1/emrakul-the-aeons-torn)? Not even a cheeky [Smog](https://scryfall.com/card/ons/132/chain-of-smog)/[Wife](https://scryfall.com/card/stx/86/sedgemoor-witch)?

I dunno. Like I've mentioned before, I've had more success with these midrangey cheat decks than the all-in ones, but cards like [Bomba](https://scryfall.com/card/lcc/86/broadside-bombardiers) and [Voidwalker](https://scryfall.com/card/tdc/176/dauthi-voidwalker) are disparate enough to be agro oil to our reanimator plan water.

Well, anyway. Everyone has a plan until pirate goblins punch them in the mouth. Gunna stick by taking the powerful cards here.

# Trophy Esper Archon
![Deck #5](/images/blogs/msh-drafts/deck5.png)

Speaking of reani-midrange, we're back to Esper for another light cheaty deck.

Here it's just the [Archon](https://scryfall.com/card/mh2/75/archon-of-cruelty) and a couple ways to bring it back.  This is much more in line with how I'm hoping to build these decks. Discard to good threats like [Ledger Shredder](https://scryfall.com/card/snc/46/ledger-shredder) or [Frog](https://scryfall.com/card/mh3/199/psychic-frog) and reanimate with all-rounders like [Emporer of Bones](https://scryfall.com/card/mh3/90/emperor-of-bones).

Not a new Marvel card, but a hero nevertheless - I should give [Super Spider-Man](https://scryfall.com/card/spm/155/superior-spider-man) a bit more respect. Four mana's a lot for a reanimation spell, but there's a higher floor here suping up something small like a [Malcolm](https://scryfall.com/card/lci/63/malcolm-alluring-scoundrel).

# Trophy Esper Tempo
![Deck #6](/images/blogs/msh-drafts/deck6.png)

Back on familiar ground with an Esper midrange deck. You know the drill: strong flash threats, disruption, and an [Aang](https://scryfall.com/card/tla/204/aang-swift-savior-aang-and-la-oceans-fury) that goes around way too late.

We opened an insane pack two: [Lotus](https://scryfall.com/card/2ed/233/black-lotus), [Time Walk](https://scryfall.com/card/2ed/84/time-walk), and [Recall](https://scryfall.com/card/2ed/48/ancestral-recall)! Jeez, how do you pick!

Lotus might be the best card in the cube, but we don't have big, snowbally threats and burning it on a counterspell seems weak. Time Walk is great, but likewise, doesn't do much with a hand full of interaction. Ultimately, I  decided Recall fit best into our gameplan: we could hold up mana, trade resources, and refill our hand.

I dunno! I'll be thinking about this for a while. We got the trophy, so if I guess I made the right call!

# Trophy Monow Blue
![Deck #7](/images/blogs/msh-drafts/deck7.png)

Sticking with the previous plan, another temp deck.

Bit of a funny draft. We started with some strong blue cards, then just kept taking them! We saw some passed over some strong cards in other colours, but never picked up the fixing, so we stuck with a couple solid white cards we snagged on the fringes.

I wouldn't _choose_ to be so locked in on one colour - we were really hard up for removal - but it worked out okay. A couple wraths in the board really shored up our game against creature decks and [The One Ring](https://scryfall.com/card/ltr/246/the-one-ring) kept us going against the rest.

Another not-quite-new card I was thinking about is [Appa](https://scryfall.com/card/tla/10/appa-steadfast-guardian), the not-quite-[Resto](https://scryfall.com/card/inr/38/restoration-angel). Not the most necessary card here, but I was pleased with the flexibility of re-triggering some ETBs and resetting the Ring. Maybe he's another one I should take higher. Yip yip!

# Trophy Same Ol' Same Ol'
![Deck #8](/images/blogs/msh-drafts/deck8.png)

Yet another blue-white tempo deck! I tried, I really did. Look at poor first-pick [Minsc & Boo](https://scryfall.com/card/clb/285/minsc-&-boo-timeless-heroes), hanging out in the sideboard.

I moved into blue over [Riddler](https://scryfall.com/card/eoe/72/quantum-riddler) of all things. I was aiming for some kind of Temur beatdown deck, but no such luck. Oh well, these tempo decks continue to be kind and who am I to scorn fate's tender kiss?

Shout out to the last opponent who had a sick black-white death-and-taxes kind of deck. Really cool, and absolutely tore my hands apart with [Cloak and Dagger](https://scryfall.com/card/msh/211/cloak-and-dagger-entwined). We got real lucky to draw into a [Wrath](https://scryfall.com/card/cmm/70/wrath-of-god) with a stolen [Skullclamp](https://scryfall.com/card/msc/210/skullclamp) right before they demolished us in the last game.

# Closing the Comic Book
And that wraps up Marvel!

I dunno, even setting aside my distaste for the dastardly do-gooders, I wasn't too wowed. [Cloak and Dagger](https://scryfall.com/card/msh/211/cloak-and-dagger-entwined) was better than expected, [Night Nurse](https://scryfall.com/card/msh/26/night-nurse-healer-of-heroes) is an upgrade to Sam, [The Wonderous Wasp](https://scryfall.com/card/msh/84/the-wondrous-wasp) was a serviceable tempo pickup, and I saw [Batrock](https://scryfall.com/card/msc/49/batroc-the-leaper) get in a good kick or two.

I guess at the end of the day, that's not a complaint - I'm happier with the heroes staying off the pages. See you in the funny papers!